// mymac on Cloudflare: the builder page as static assets, plus a small Worker (src/worker.js)
// that renders the bash scripts from the code in the URL. It stores nothing: no KV, no D1, no
// logs of its own. There is no build step; wrangler bundles the Worker, and public/ is served
// as it is.
//
//   npx wrangler dev                  local, http://localhost:8787
//
// Deployed by .github/workflows/deploy.yml on every push to main (the first deploy was by
// hand, 2026-11-16). Manual fallback, from a checkout of main and only when that workflow is
// broken:
//
//   cf-run npx --yes wrangler@4.116.0 deploy
//
// A ROUTE, not a custom domain. stoatworks-labs.com is at Cloudflare's limit of 100 Workers
// custom domains per zone (error 100122), so `custom_domain: true` would upload a Worker that
// nothing serves. A route has no such limit but needs a proxied DNS record to exist first,
// which wrangler does not create: `mymac` is an AAAA 100:: record, proxied, made through the
// API on 2026-11-16. Delete that record and the site goes dark while deploys still succeed.
{
  "name": "mymac",
  "main": "src/worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-01",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public",
    "binding": "ASSETS"
  },
  "observability": { "enabled": false },
  "routes": [{ "pattern": "mymac.stoatworks-labs.com/*", "zone_name": "stoatworks-labs.com" }]
}
